        <body>
            <div xml:id="d626">

                <pb facs="0673" n="555" xml:id="pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/6236: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-17T10:00:00-05:45">March 17, 1929—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>72. Brigade headquarters reports that on March 14 marine patrol encountered a
                    group of bandits at Department of Chinandega, two miles west of San Juan de
                    Limay. One bandit killed. On March 15th combined marine and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">voluntario</hi> force encountered bandits in the same
                    vicinity, killing four and capturing three. No marine or <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >voluntario</hi> casualties. Marines believe that bandits constituted
                    Salgado’s main group and that they crossed into Honduras about March 16th.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tegucigalpa.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
